[node name="TitleRichTextLabel" parent="Left/MarginContainer/Nodes" parent_id_path=PackedInt32Array(1644936578) index="1" unique_id=1098942946]
text = "[b][u]The Secret Code: How does it work ?[/u][/b]"

[node name="Label1" type="Label" parent="Left/MarginContainer/Nodes" parent_id_path=PackedInt32Array(1644936578) index="2" unique_id=2117813230]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(1, 0)
layout_mode = 2
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 15
text = "As mentioned earlier, the secret code is a string of characters of unknown length. But we know that it is long and random.
To put it simply, it is a sequence of many characters.

The safe is equipped with a system that generates a new secret code every time someone enters the room. Two phases then come into play.
The first phase is the generation of the secret code. It is entirely random in two respects:
- The safe itself chooses 90% of the elements of the secret code;
- The safe wants a high level of security, so it knows it can’t rely on itself to create the entire secret code. It therefore fetches data from elsewhere—data that doesn’t depend on it—and incorporates it into the secret code. At least, that is, if that darn web browser doesn’t interfere with the safe’s proper functioning.

Then, once that is done, the second phase can begin."
autowrap_mode = 3

[node name="PagesCountRichTextLabel" parent="Right/MarginContainer/Nodes" parent_id_path=PackedInt32Array(1257509253) index="0" unique_id=1838195359]
